  ["I've heard it said that Deneb Walker, holed up in Stromgarde, has a book that is sure to help improve your First Aid techniques."]=3,
},
[5153]={ -- Jormund Stonebrow
  ["Ah, this Darnassian fabric is the finest!"]=1,
  ["Well, aren't you the smarty-pants? Ye know more than I do, I can tell ye that! Don't go getting' a big head, but if ye want to keep learnin', have a chat with Georgio Bolero in Stormwind. They say he knows his tailorin'!"]=2,
  ["I don't have time to babysit! Go talk to me assistant, Uthrar!"]=3,
},
[5157]={ -- Gimble Thistlefuzz
  ["Who are you? What do you want from me?"]=1,
  ["What do I look like, the Grand Poobah of enchanters? Your skills require the guidance of an Artisan! Go find Kitta Firewind at the Tower of Azora."]=2,
  ["You're joking, right? I believe you're looking for the OTHER short fellow, Thonys Pillarstone. He's downstairs. Now skedaddle!"]=3,
},
[5159]={ -- Daryl Riknussun
  ["I keep 'em fed, kid. Yep, Daryl Riknussun, at yer service."]=1,
  ["Cooking is a life long pursuit and I see we share the same passion!"]=2,
  ["Seek out Shandrina in Silverwind Refuge. She can sell you the 'Expert Cookbook'."]=3,
},
[5164]={ -- Grumnus Steelshaper
  ["Ye bothered me for that? Ye'd be better off strapping a dead rabbit to yer back and running through a Troll's den than wearing that piece of garbage."]=1,
  ["adventurer, was it? That is a mighty fine piece of work ye have there. I'll take ye on, train ye how to make armor fit fer King Magni himself."]=2,
},
[5165]={ -- Hulfdan Blackbeard
  ["He grows fatter and more corrupt with each passing day. Ye can smell the stink comin' off o' his body. He be dirty, an' I dun just mean he be needin' a wash. Enough babblin' from Hulfdan. Where did ye come from and how can me help ye, $c?"]=1,
  ["Can't help ya, adventurer. I only train rogues."]=2,
  ["I got something for you, adventurer. Looks important."]=3,
  ["He grows fatter and more corrupt with each passing day. Ye can smell the stink comin' off o' his body. He be dirty, an' I dun just mean he be needin' a wash. Enough babblin' from Hulfdan. Where did ye come from and how can me help ye, rogue?"]=4,
